# Onec Platform Fact Check

This is optional guidance for the main onec-context skill. Load
[the reference](reference.md) when this topic is relevant. Executable tools live
in the main skill or an exported bundle, not in this supplemental directory.
Resolve their actual location before running a command. Do not assume that
`onec-context` is installed on PATH.

Identify the exact platform version and full identifier, such as
`HTTPСоединение.Получить`. Query the platform pack with `--exact --version` and
`--json`. Short global names are supported; prefer the full name for members.
Do not assume English aliases have the same exact-match behavior as stored names.

Read `--detail full` before asserting parameter order, return types, execution
context or restrictions. Inspect the actual fields present. The extractor may
not have preserved every fact in the original page. Search `api_examples`
separately when an example is needed; examples can be separate records.

Without `--exact`, the reader tries an exact match and then lexical FTS5 search.
A nearby search result is a candidate to inspect, not proof of the requested API.
No match does not prove absence from the language. Do not transfer a fact from
one platform version to another without matching evidence.

Cite the topic and version. If the source is incomplete, identify the remaining
question and inspect the locally available original documentation. Generated
code still needs the project's diagnostics and relevant tests. A help lookup
is not a successful compilation or execution.
